From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:52:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Ask fixes an agent's refused image and spent free
 model by itself
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- A provider that refuses a request with an image in it (HTTP 400 "Failed
  to read HTTP message", "does not support image input", …): Ask runs the
  turn again at once, text only (Meridian's bridge leaves screenshots out,
  OpenCode gets no tools), what came so far is replaced, and that agent
  and model stay text only (prefs kAiTextOnly). Nobody sets anything.
- OpenCode on its own free model, out of it, with a model of the person's
  set up in OpenCode: the error carries one button, "Use your model …",
  which picks it for OpenCode (SetCliModel, prefs kAiModels) and asks
  again. Without one: another AI from the menu; never "try again later",
  never a file to edit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
